#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:5
#: 371d0f37e1734a459f6c29ce52e0ed8c
msgid "AutoTrim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:7
#: 86b61c530aea4a7bb251d4cd6796e132
msgid "Wind of course has a strong effect on your copter and will push it around. However you may also find that while flying in stabilize mode, even in a windless environment your copter tends to always drift away in the same direction. This can largely be corrected using the \"Save Trim\" or \"Automatic Trim\" functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:11
#: dde3e2919d4543b3a073ed19409dcd37
msgid "For most users this procedure is not necessary because the :ref:`accelerometer calibration <common-accelerometer-calibration>` does a good job of setting the trim values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:14
#: 43b2c0a4d5b84e4586c1ed41b68deabc
msgid "AHRS AutoTrim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:16
#: f9b543ae655f4e61b41abeeee43f0c9f
msgid "With AHRS AutoTrim the roll and pitch corrections are captured as you fly in a stable hover. Setup a :ref:`common-auxiliary-functions` switch to \"In Flight AHRS trim adjust\" (\"182\"). We will use CH7 in the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:18
#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:51
#: e3c49cb5fa0d45a597e009511de6110c
#: ffe0ae10cb894c09a792e4e614044de1
msgid "Check that your CH7 switch goes above 1800 on the MissionPlanner's Setup > Mandatory Hardware > Radio Calibration screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:23
#: 58e6d28fde5f46e9b92714f616c641a6
msgid "Set the CH7 Option to \"AHRS AutoTrim\" on the Software > Copter Pids screen and press the \"Write Params\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:25
#: a3ad5c5b00e6471691e813e00ed2666a
msgid "Find a wind free environment with sufficient space to fly your copter without crashing into something."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:27
#: 7b60c193e1454a4981c7b94831c9b137
msgid "Put the vehicle in manual Stabilize/AltHold mode or a position hold Loiter/PosHold mode (recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:29
#: f3aa1b4cbea44d61889127fffb934270
msgid "Arm the vehicle and lift into a hover. The vehicle must be flying in order to enable autotrim. Flip the switch that you setup (CH7) to its High position (>1800us). \"Autotrim running\" message will be sent to the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:31
#: 2648624821e14b148ac0df7cd9a31086
msgid "If in a manual mode, fly your copter for about 25 seconds in a stable hover in position, keeping it from drifting with the pitch and roll sticks. As the trim is adjusted, less and less corrections with the sticks will be required. If using a position hold mode, take off and let the copter hover in place while not touching the sticks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:33
#: 5ce3dd379af64c51a739ecacfa183c68
msgid "Once satisfied, flip the switch low, saving the trims, and land. \"Trim save\" message will be sent to the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:35
#: e8547e07254848ba8e90cd67ad3ff616
msgid "Take off in AltHold mode and check if your copter is flying level now. If not repeat steps 4 - 7 again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:39
#: 1de749d905274e129b5f089b41c404b3
msgid "You can manually set the trim by modifying the :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_X <AHRS_TRIM_X>` and :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_Y <AHRS_TRIM_Y>`. Roll trim is :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_X <AHRS_TRIM_X>`, Pitch trim is :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_Y <AHRS_TRIM_Y>`. Both values are in radians with left roll and forward pitch being negative numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:43
#: 00fe9c4fadc14a4ea6ca2323d552ab3a
msgid "It is nearly impossible to get rid of all drift so that your copter remains completely motionless without any input. It may be preferable to yaw the copter 90 degrees and holding that orientation for about 6-7 seconds each time so that any external disturbances will get cancelled out, resulting in a better trim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:46
#: e51e89494d474232b0bd0170556ef5ad
msgid "Save Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:47
#: cb97d1a854b243c39d3020f3bc3a6c85
msgid "the above AHRS AutoTrim method is preferred since it does not involve moving transmitter trims after RC calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:49
#: a501f260c46a454ebf30469a60f060ee
msgid "Save trim involves essentially transferring your radio transmitter's trims into the autopilot's AHRS trim (the :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_X <AHRS_TRIM_X>` and :ref:`AHRS_TRIM_Y <AHRS_TRIM_Y>` parameters), the same values that the AHRS AutoTrim method above adjusts. Normally, once :ref:`common-accelerometer-calibration` is done, you never want to change the transmitter's trims, but in this case it is done **temporarily**. The \"Save Trim\" function (\"5\") is assigned to any free RC channel, usually a switch based one, using an :ref:`common-auxiliary-functions`. For the example below, Channel 7 will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:56
#: 67eb60a6fc764be793bdcd738863422a
msgid "Set the RC7 Option to Save Trim in the Config > Extended Tuning screen and press the \"Write Params\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:61
#: 4fbd89bd48684dbdb394354eab0689d7
msgid "With your CH7 switch in the off (Low) position, fly your copter in Stabilize mode and use your transmitters's roll and pitch trim to get it flying level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:63
#: fedc84c235ef4394b9a070f14c9e5c90
msgid "Land and put your throttle to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:65
#: 46160802cca942d982af3adcd394283b
msgid "Release the roll and pitch sticks and switch the CH7 switch high for at least 1 second.  The words \"Trim saved\" should appear in the MP's Flight Data screen's Messages tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:67
#: a85411b1f0fb4c199bb9e0ea5b76196a
msgid "Reset your transmitters roll and pitch trims back to the center and fly again and it should fly level now. If it does not repeat steps 3, 4 & 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:70
#: 4a19bf9eea26460ba46b5b8f9182f472
msgid "Desktop method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:72
#: 04b0e3f40ef2432c8012b737025d4241
msgid "The trim can also be updated by setting the vehicle level, connecting to the Mission Planner (or perhaps other ground stations) and selecting Initial Setup, Mandatory Hardware, Accel Calibration and pushing the lower \"Calibrate Level\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/autotrim.rst:80
#: 7b1c3aa927a44cfeb2cd849f71f81791
msgid "Please note though that making the HUD level while the vehicle is on the ground does not necessarily mean it won't drift horizontally while flying because of other small frame issues including the flight controller not being perfectly level on the frame, CG placement, an/ord slightly tilted motors."
msgstr ""
